'' RUN: '!"C:\\Users\\x"' is decoded: the 'U' after an escaped backslash is text, not a
'' unicode escape, which left the whole literal undecoded with both slashes in it.
'' Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/escaped-backslash-u.bas -o tests/codegen/escapedbackslashu.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/escapedbackslashu.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: C:\Users\x
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  10
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: C:\Users       8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2            65            66
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1            A
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  4
